I am applying for the Senior Data Analyst role at MongoDB in Gurugram.

Throughout my work as a data analyst, I have focused on building resilient da=
ta pipelines, scalable data models, and automated reporting systems. At Black=
 Piano, I architected 18 automated ETL pipelines feeding Google Cloud BigQuer=
y across 18 industry sectors, while engineering a self-healing data-quality a=
gent powered by Gemini to resolve missing records and validate pipeline accur=
acy. At Pi Software Solutions, I developed production Python data pipelines u=
sing an internal package for automated BigQuery access across 10 client dashb=
oards, delivering over 30 analytical industry reports. My core technical stre=
ngths include advanced SQL, Google Cloud Platform, data modeling, ETL orchest=
ration, and reporting with Tableau and Looker Studio.

Prior to these roles, I spent nine years at Optum conducting federal enrollme=
nt transaction audits for Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services compliance=
. In that role, I applied zero-tolerance quality gates to high-volume transac=
tion datasets, generated audit-ready documentation, and produced discrepancy =
reports. That rigorous compliance and audit background underpins how I manage=
 data quality, enforce validation rules, and structure dependable data models=
 in production environments.

I admire MongoDB for setting the standard in modern developer data platforms =
and empowering teams to build high-performance applications at global scale.

I welcome the opportunity to discuss how my SQL, Google Cloud, and data model=
ing experience can deliver value to the analytics team at MongoDB.

